<body>
  <h1>Family Dashboard Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: November 17, 2026</p>

  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Family Dashboard is a private household application
    designed to display Google Calendar appointments,
    manage chores, and organize grocery lists.
  </p>

  <h2>Information Accessed</h2>
  <p>
    With the account owner's authorization, Family Dashboard
    accesses Google Calendar event information, including
    event titles, dates, times, and descriptions.
  </p>

  <h2>How Information Is Used</h2>
  <p>
    Google Calendar information is used to display
    appointments and activities within the dashboard.
    Calendar access is read-only.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Storage and Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    Calendar events are retrieved from Google Calendar
    and displayed within the household dashboard.
    Calendar data is not sold or shared with advertisers.
    The application does not maintain a separate
    permanent database of Google Calendar events.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Google account authorization is handled through
    Google's OAuth authentication system.
    Access credentials are not published on this website.
  </p>

  <h2>Revoking Access</h2>
  <p>
    Users may revoke the application's Google account
    permissions through their Google Account settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy inquiries may be directed to the application
    developer through the support email displayed on
    the Google OAuth consent screen.
  </p>

  <p><a href="index.html">Return to Home</a></p>
</body>
</html>
